  "steps": [
    "Preheat the air fryer to 400°F.",
    "Toss the chicken with the baking soda, cornstarch, pepper, paprika, salt, ginger, garlic powder and red pepper flakes. Spray all sides generously with cooking spray.",
    "Air fry in a single layer about 14 minutes, shaking the basket halfway, until golden and the thickest piece reads 165°F.",
    "Meanwhile, whisk all the sauce ingredients together until the cornstarch dissolves.",
    "Pour the sauce into a nonstick pan over medium heat and cook, stirring constantly, until thick and glossy, about 5 minutes.",
    "Toss the chicken in the sauce. Serve over rice with orange slices."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Baking soda on the chicken helps it brown and stay tender.",
    "The two red pepper flake amounts make it spicy; halve them for mild.",
    "Most published air fryer orange chicken sweetens with honey instead of a sugar substitute (Supergolden Bakes uses 1/4 cup honey); 1 to 2 tbsp honey works here if you prefer.",
    "Macros per half, without rice: 322 cal, 51.6g protein. With rice: 492 cal, 55.6g protein."
